            <ArticleTitle>Metal-assisted exfoliation of few-layer black phosphorus with high yield.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7cc08488a</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We introduce a metal-assisted exfoliation method to produce few-layer black phosphorus with the lateral size larger than 50 μm and the area 100 times larger than those exfoliated using the normal &quot;scotch-tape&quot; technique. Using a field effect transistor it was found the hole mobility is 68.6 cm2 V-1 s-1 and the current on/off ratio can reach about 2 × 105.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
